{
  "title": "Hotel (board game) — Reception",
  "date": "03-29",
  "text": "On BoardGameGeek, it has an average rating of 5.5/10 based on roughly 5000 reviews. In the February 1988 issue of The Games Machine (Issue 3), the reviewer said that \"Hotel, although aimed at eight-years-old and up, can become involved and time consuming. It proves immense fun to play, and the board and accessories are such an attractive sight it is quite a disappointment when the whole thing gets packed up in its box again. Concentration is a must although actual brainpower is not over-used. A worthwhile game to play with friends and a good supply of food 'n 'drink.\"",
